v5.3.0
Radon Player 5.3.0: The big check-up, and eleven new things
- **Downloads carry on after a restart, and the ones that didn't come are kept (the phone and the PC):** songs still waiting to download when the app closes are picked up again the next time it opens. Songs that failed or couldn't be found are listed at the top of **Downloads**, each with why, with **Try again** (all, or one by a tap) and **Clear**. Before, both were forgotten the moment the app closed.
- **Battery saver (Settings › General):** the phone's Visualizer widget draws 15 times a second for 30, and the lyrics, mood and listening scans wait until the device is plugged in. On the phone it also comes on by itself while Android's own battery saver is on. On the PC it only holds the scans back on a laptop running on its battery (a desktop PC is always plugged in, and the PC has no home-screen widget to slow).
- **What a Refresh found (the phone and the PC):** reading your music again when you ask now ends with a count: how many songs are new, changed or gone, and on the PC any chosen folder that isn't connected.
- **Compilations are one album (the phone and the PC):** the read of your music now keeps each file's album artist, track and disc number. An album whose songs are by different artists (a compilation, a soundtrack) is one album under its album artist, not one for each artist; and an album's songs are put in order without opening every file, so album pages open faster.
- **Preview a sync (the phone and the PC):** **Preview**, beside Sync now, shows what a sync would change on each device (which playlists gain or lose songs, favorites, the rest) before anything is changed, with Sync now right there. Both apps need this version.
- **Is this a car? (the phone):** while a Bluetooth output plays, Settings › Playback asks whether it is a car, for headphones named like one or a car named like nothing. A car gets the car's EQ and counts for Car always wins. The PC has no car outputs, so this is the phone's only.
- **Reset sound to defaults (the phone and the PC):** Settings › Sound quality: the playing output's equalizer back to flat with Bass, Treble and Boost at 0 and no headphone correction; crossfeed, mono, Detail and loudness compensation off; balance and tilt to the middle. Your saved presets and other outputs' EQs are kept.
- **Record slow frames (Settings › General, the phone and the PC):** for lag you can feel but not show. Turn it on, do what stutters, turn it off and Copy: it notes how many frames took too long, the worst, and the screen each was on. It stops by itself after ten minutes.
- **Names that stay whole (Settings › Scanner › Last.fm & your stats, the phone and the PC):** an artist with a comma or “&” in their own name (Tyler, The Creator; Earth, Wind & Fire; a few more are built in) is never taken for two artists, in artist lists, pages and stats. Add any the app splits wrongly, one a line.
- **Each playlist keeps its own sort (the phone and the PC):** the sort you pick in a playlist (a smart playlist or a mood list too) is kept for that playlist. One you never sorted follows the last sort you picked, as before.
- **What a preset holds (Personalization):** under Save as a preset, a line says what a preset saved now would keep: the look, theme, layout, effects, visualizers, visualizer colour, Wrapped and lyrics card styles.
- **The phone's Visualizer widget at 30 frames a second**, up from about 8, and it rests after five minutes of running (it never did: any song change started it again).
- **Where you were in a song is kept over a restart (the phone and the PC):** the app opens at the same place in the song, not its start.
- **A music folder that isn't there is “not connected” (the PC mostly):** a drive unplugged no longer takes its songs out of your playlists, favorites and queue. They are left alone until the folder has been missing for two days and three reads.
- **A PC file keeps every artist it names:** only the first was read (“Post Malone, Swae Lee” became “Post Malone”). Your files are read once more.
- **Sync and backup put right:** a sync whose answer never reached the phone no longer undoes the PC's changes at the next one; a backup put back on a paired device starts the next sync afresh instead of rolling the other device back; backups hold the listening diary, mood lists, repeats and playlist covers too; each device's own look is no longer sent, so a second sync says nothing changed; pairing rests a minute after five wrong codes.
- **New releases put right:** an artist that couldn't be looked up once is no longer dropped for good; a look made offline no longer empties the list or counts as done; where each release plays from is remembered between runs.
- **Lyrics put right:** lyrics you typed are what the Lyrics tab shows after Save (the web's had replaced them); a lyrics or mood scan run offline no longer writes songs down as having none, and stops and says so; auto-sync keeps the words you typed.
- **Playback put right:** Play after the queue ended starts it again (the phone did nothing); a stream that broke no longer leaves the player stuck; adding to the queue no longer cuts the playing song short; Previous twice while paused goes back a song; the Shuffle pills shuffle; on the PC, `queue FILE` and `next FILE` add to the queue.
- **Sound put right:** loudness compensation stays off on a new install; editing another output's EQ no longer changes what is playing; on the PC an EQ band above what the song can carry no longer silences the whole EQ; bit-perfect left on with no DAC no longer blocks Speed and crossfade; headphones such as Audio-Technica are no longer taken for a car.
- **Smoother and lighter (the phone and the PC):** names are tidied once, not at every comparison of a sort; Now playing no longer redraws twice a second; the PC reads a list's covers at the size they are drawn; the phone as the PC's remote asks every 5 seconds off the screen, not every second; the screen check sleeps with the screen off; the DJ's first set is no longer made every half hour for someone who never uses it; Tidal's sign-in running out is said, once.
- **Smaller fixes:** “Searching…” no longer sticks; the YouTube fallback keeps to the song's version (no live take for a studio song); presets save the visualizer around the cover and keep earlier edits when several are edited; Preset Shuffle and Presets by time of day are one at a time; the DJ talks in the middle of its early sets again and its second and third sets no longer share songs; smart playlists with time rules move on through the day; a playlist sent to the phone is kept until it has it.

